-- S18 -- «B7»: A FUNCTION THAT RETURNS A RECORD -- WRITABLE, AND IT DOES NOT
--        REACH THE PROOF.
--
-- `FRAGMENTE.md` «B7»: *"No struct and no array literal in `expr`. A function
-- therefore cannot produce a `structty`; tuple return and `reply(EP, [ … ])`
-- fall with it."* Cited at F4, F5 and F6.
--
-- **THE CHECKER AND THE EMITTER BOTH TAKE IT.** The braced spelling the
-- fragment wrote is refused, and the refusal names the working one:
--
--   return Completion { id: k, len: n };
--     [P037] Gabbro has no braced record literal
--            = instead of `P { a: 1, b: 2 }` one writes `P(a: 1, b: 2)`
--            = the field list of a declaration IS its constructor
--
--   return Completion(id: k, len: n);     0 errors, 0 hints
--   gabbro emit                           rc=0, and the C is
--                                         `return (Completion){ .id = k, .len = n };`
--   return Completion(k, n);              [M107] its constructor names its fields
--
-- WHERE IT STOPS IS THE THIRD TOOL, AND THAT IS THE ROW:
--
--   gabbro lean-g messung/schreibprobe/S18-verbund-als-wert.gab
--   [LG002] the result of fertig is the record Completion, and a record has NO
--   `Ty`: `Typen.lean` §1 is `int`, `bool`, `opt`, `sum`, `grund`, `never`,
--   `fl`, `fnptr`, `ptr` -- there is no product. A record travels as a CARRIER
--   (a `Tab` with `count 1`, reached through a pointer, `Syntax.lean` §1/§9),
--   and that is built; it does NOT travel as a value, so a result, a parameter
--   or a `let` of record type has no form at all. Passing a
--   `ptr<normal, r> Completion` has one
--
-- So the program is writable, compiles, and is OUTSIDE the goal theorem. That
-- is a different thing from "cannot be written", and it is the thing
-- `OFFEN.md` O15 and O16 priced on 2026-09-15 and REFUSED: the `Ty`
-- constructor gains ZERO of 113 corpus programs, and the C side of an
-- aggregate value (O16) is owed by a form the specification already HAS
-- (`tagged type` constructors, `beispiele/120`).
--
-- «B7»'s other two halves: an array literal exists as a `const` initialiser
-- (`constwert = constexpr | arraylit`, lane 111, `beispiele/123`), and a
-- `tagged type` value has a constructor since lane 167 (O8, `beispiele/120`).

module schreibprobe::verbund_wert {

type Completion = { id : u32, len : u32, };

impl fn fertig(k : u32, n : u32) -> Completion
    effects { pure }
    costs   <= 8 ops
{
    return Completion(id: k, len: n);
}

}
